_score_int_coverage":7.8,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":3.6001230390649033,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":8.9,"_gate_accruals":-0.03599862731640357,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":62.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.4966388829260474,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.009053477027526298,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.056262332563100315,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":28.1,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.4349928441700919,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.15148481691916918,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.00013082445177303725,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":39.9,"_gate_rev_durability":0.07665701027771288,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":63.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.13773138557556375,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.008776318304306474,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":41.2,"_gate_fund_growth":0.13059906761821802,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.08444046413214815,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.029386155741718656,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":86.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00436297333376746,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.04463,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":29.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"NRG Energy, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an energy and home services company in the United States and Canada. It operates through the Texas, East, West/Other, Vivint Smart Home, and Corporate Activities segments. The company offers retail electricity, energy management, demand response and virtual power plant programs, carbon offsets, smart home security, and automation services. It also offers system power, distributed and backup generation, energy storage, energy management, renewable and low-carbon products, and carbon management solutions for large business and commercial customers; a cloud-based home platform, including hardware, software, sales, installation, customer service, technical support, and professional monitoring solutions; and generation portfolio includes fossil fuel and renewable generation assets diversified by fuel type and dispatch level, with ongoing development of new natural gas and renewable projects. In addition, the company trades in power, natural gas, and related products; environmental products; weather products; and financial products, including forwards, futures, options, and swaps. It offers its products and services under the NRG, Reliant, Direct Energy, Green Mountain Energy, and Vivint. It serves residential, commercial, government, industrial, data center, and wholesale customers. NRG Energy, Inc. was founded in 1989 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert J. Gaudette | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 16K people. Revenue per employee of $1.8M ranks in the top quartile among Utilities peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $46K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["NRG Energy, Inc. is a large-cap utilities business with a $20.4B market cap on $30.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 7% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $766M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.1pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 15% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4308922.2},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 13% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 44% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Utilities peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Are Strong Earnings Altering The Investment Case For NRG Energy (NRG)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-nrg/nrg-energy/news/are-strong-earnings-altering-the-investment-case-for-nrg-ene","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572770.41,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.94,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"589,678 NRG Energy, Inc. $NRG Shares Purchased by Eurizon Capital SGR S.p.A.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/589678-nrg-energy-inc-nrg-shares-purchased-by-eurizon-capital-sgr-s-p-a.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794561221.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.955,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NRG Energy Inc (NRG) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: $4 Billion Asset Sale, $3 Billion ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/a